# nexus-estate-platform-engine — Agent Rules

This repository is a Go modular monorepo: one go.mod, bounded modules, three
initial deployables (`cmd/search`, `cmd/engine`, `cmd/worker`).

- Inspect the repository and current diff before editing. Prefer small commits;
  run tests after each structural commit.
- Keep entry points thin. Wire dependencies in `internal/app`; place domain
  behavior and adapters in the bounded module that owns them.
- Put technical client/bootstrap concerns in `internal/platform`. Platform code
  must not import bounded modules; avoid cross-module infrastructure imports.
- Keep one Go module. Do not create a microservice/repository per domain, empty
  future modules, speculative interfaces or generic BaseService/Manager/Utils.
- Use contract-first development with `proto/search/v1/search.proto`; regenerate
  checked-in Go using `make proto`. No external contract repository is assumed.
- Preserve Search wire package, RPC names, field numbers, port 50052, index/query
  behavior and optional Redis fallback during foundation work.
- Propagate context, close resources, and use bounded graceful shutdown. Search
  readiness requires Elasticsearch, never the optional cache.
- Build separate images for nexus-search, nexus-engine and nexus-worker. Derive
  the Go toolchain version from go.mod and keep direct Docker defaults aligned.
- Run gofmt, vet, golangci-lint v2, race tests, tidy verification and binary builds
  before proposing merge. Do not auto-commit tidy changes in CI.
- Keep cluster mutations in the GitOps repository. Never merge a PR automatically
  or delete old Search images/deployments before staging verification.
- Add Pricing/Billing/Scheduler or other modules only for authorized real features.
